#====================================================================
# Draft: glib/2.88.3 conan components are named glib/gobject/gio —
#        "glib::glib-2.0" in component requires aborts PkgConfigDeps
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-LIBXMLB-GLIB-COMPONENT-NAMING
trigger_tool:           conan|PkgConfigDeps|package_info
phase:                  packaging
error_signature:        Component 'glib::glib-2.0' not found in 'glib' package requirement|The direct dependency .* is not used by any

severity:               2
category:               conan, gnome, packaging
match_keywords:         glib, glib-2.0, component, requires, PkgConfigDeps, pkg_config_name, not found, package requirement, gio-2.0, gobject-2.0

title:                  glib/2.88.3 declares conan components named glib/gobject/gio (pkg_config_name maps them to glib-2.0/gio-2.0), so cross-package component requires must be "glib::glib" — "glib::glib-2.0" aborts PkgConfigDeps generation

root_cause:             The glib/2.88.3 recipe (archives/g/glib/2.88.3) registers
                        cpp_info.components["glib"|"gobject"|"gio"|...] and maps each
                        to its pkg-config name via set_property("pkg_config_name",
                        "glib-2.0"|"gio-2.0"|...). The earlier glib/2.84.0.1 recipe
                        instead named the components "glib-2.0"/"gobject-2.0"/"gio-2.0"
                        directly. Recipes written against the old naming list
                        requires = ["glib::glib-2.0", ...]; with glib/2.88.3 the
                        PkgConfigDeps generator (or conan's dependency validation)
                        raises "Component 'glib::glib-2.0' not found in 'glib'
                        package requirement" at generate()/package_info() time.
                        Related: every direct requirement must be consumed by some
                        component's requires, otherwise "The direct dependency
                        'liblzma' is not used by any '(cpp_info/components).requires'".

affected_scope:         Any recipe requiring the shared glib/2.88.3 package with
                        component-style package_info (GNOME ecosystem: libxmlb,
                        libsoup3-style consumers, gtk-era migrations). Verified
                        instance: libxmlb 0.3.19.

verification_cmd:       conan create archives/l/libxmlb/0.3.19 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           component-name-not-pc-name
rec_description:        Reference the conan component NAME, not the pkg-config name:
                        requires = ["glib::glib", "glib::gobject", "glib::gio"];
                        the pkg_config_name properties on glib's components still
                        emit glib-2.0.pc/gio-2.0.pc for pkg-config consumers. List
                        EVERY direct requirement (flat packages referenced as
                        pkg::pkg, e.g. "liblzma::liblzma", "zstd::zstd") in the
                        component requires or conan fails with "direct dependency
                        not used by any components".
rec_command:            lib.requires = ["glib::glib", "glib::gobject", "glib::gio", "liblzma::liblzma", "zstd::zstd"]
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               package_info() in archives/l/libxmlb/0.3.19/conanfile.py

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      no-component-flat-cppinfo
fallback_description:   Drop components entirely and set flat cpp_info.libs with
                        pkg_config_name (json-glib style). Works but loses per-
                        component dependency propagation for CMakeDeps consumers.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       requires.*glib::glib-2\.0
forbid_1_reason:        glib/2.88.3 component names are glib/gobject/gio; the
                        ::glib-2.0 form aborts the generator.
forbid_1_consequence:   conan create fails at PkgConfigDeps generate() with
                        "Component 'glib::glib-2.0' not found".

principles:

causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:             E537
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
